**RE: Request for a binding country of origin ruling — Kobalt 12.5-amp heat gun, model 5208257**

Dear Sir or Madam:

Pursuant to 19 C.F.R. Part 177, [REQUESTER NAME] respectfully requests a binding ruling on the country of origin of Kobalt 12.5-amp heat gun, model 5208257 for purposes of marking and the application of trade remedies, including Section 301 duties.

CBP previously ruled on the current production setup: origin China (N328954). This request concerns a proposed change to that setup: make Motor-fan assembly and PCBA (SMT) in Thailand.

## Facts

The motor-fan assembly and PCBA are made in Thailand. Final assembly in Thailand.

## Issue

What is the country of origin of Kobalt 12.5-amp heat gun, model 5208257, produced as described above, under the substantial-transformation test?

## Requester's position

The requester submits that the merchandise is a product of Thailand, based on these key factors: motor-fan assembly made in Thailand and PCBA populated in Thailand. [REQUESTER TO CONFIRM AND EXPAND WITH COUNSEL.]

## Earlier CBP rulings considered

- N347421 — a comparable change where CBP found the origin moved ([rulings.cbp.gov](https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N347421)).
- N345859 — a similar change that did not alter origin; distinguish it ([rulings.cbp.gov](https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N345859)).
- N350001 ([rulings.cbp.gov](https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N350001)).

